Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:06:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/35] Paths and borders drawn into the landscape tiles

They change seldom but were drawn into every frame: on a 68060 a third
of the time of a view with many roads. The landscape tiles get them
(draw_paths_and_borders_area, with margins for the segments reaching in
from outside), Map tells its handlers when a path or an owner changes
(on_paths_changed; set_owner and del_owner only when the value changes)
and the view drops the tiles around. Only the road being built is drawn
into the frame. Viewport::paths_in_tiles = false draws them as before.

Viewport::verify_tiles: every 50 frames the tiles in view are drawn again
and compared (Video::frames_equal), tile_errors counts the differences.

640x400, Warp1260, a game with many roads: 31.3 -> 44.5 frames/s.
